---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const CALENDLY = 'https://calendly.com/russell-decisive/30min';

const title = 'Finance for wealth management firms | Decisive';
const description =
  'The AUM is growing. The practice\'s profit is a guess. We find which clients and advisors actually carry the book, in dollars, in 14 days, on guarantee.';

const traps = [
  {
    name: 'Loss Aversion',
    body: 'The large household or senior advisor you are most afraid to touch is often the one capping the practice\'s margin. The math never gets run because the answer feels dangerous.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Certainty Illusion',
    body: 'AUM that grew on market beta can feel like performance. Separate the market from the practice and the growth that was never yours shows up first, and so does the profit that is.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Status Quo',
    body: 'A fee schedule or cost nobody has revisited in years is not stable. It is margin leaking quietly, at a rate nobody has priced, because the report always looks the same.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">For wealth management and RIA firms</span>
      <h1>
        <span class="h1-line">The AUM is growing.</span>
        <span class="h1-line h1-line-accent">The practice's profit is a guess.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subhead">
        In a practice, the value hides in which clients and advisors actually carry it. <span class="dollar">We price the answer in dollars.</span> Guaranteed 3x your Diagnostic fee in recoverable value, in 14 days.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-microcopy">30 minutes with Russ. No pitch. You leave knowing where to look first.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Where the profit hides in a practice</span>
        <h2>The AUM is visible. What it earns you is not.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Client and advisor profitability, the quality of recurring fee revenue, the split between fee and commission, and what each relationship actually costs to serve: the numbers that decide where the practice's time goes. Most books grow for years without any of them run.
        </p>
        <div class="category-pull">
          Your books tell you what happened. They can't tell you what to do next.
        </div>
        <p>
          The decisions weren't wrong. You made them on the only numbers you had, and those numbers were never built to decide from. Everyone who touches your books is paid to serve something else: the filing, the close, the report. Nobody is paid to make the next call defensible, and that is the job we do.
        </p>
        <div class="delay-callout">
          We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="traps">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Where the value is trapped</div>
      <h2>Three traps behind a growing book.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.88);">
        The Six Trap Diagnostic&trade; reads your numbers through the decisions that produced them. Three of the six do the most damage in a wealth practice. The patterns are structural, not failures of the owner.
      </p>
      <div class="trap-grid">
        {traps.map((t, i) => (
          <div class="trap-card">
            <div class="trap-num">Trap {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <div class="trap-name">{t.name}</div>
            <p>{t.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="traps-footer">
        We name the stack, price each one in dollars, and turn the read into a plan. We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Proof</span>
        <h2>The mechanism reads the same across industries, because the traps do.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="worked">
        <span class="label">Professional services, $30M revenue</span>
        <h4>A clean close is not a fast one, and neither tells you where the cash is stuck.</h4>
        <p>
          Cash was trapped in a billing and close cadence nobody had revisited, and clean-looking reports masked the leak. We rebuilt the rhythm, pulled the working capital forward, and put margin on a weekly line of sight. A fee-based practice runs the same play.
        </p>
        <div class="calc">
          <div><span class="k">Working capital recovered</span><span class="v accent">$380,000</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Close time</span><span class="v">22 to 3 days</span></div>
          <div><span class="k">Margin improvement</span><span class="v">~$50,000 / mo</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 22px;">
        Anonymized by segment and revenue band until attribution is confirmed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Tiers and pricing</span>
        <h2>Find. Install. Run.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Most owners start with the 14-day Decision Diagnostic and move into the 90-Day Resolution. Pricing is banded by revenue, and the floor is $5M.
        </p>
        <p class="promise-line">
          The Diagnostic promise: at least 3x the fee in owner-accepted value identified by Day 14, or you pay nothing.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-row" style="margin-top: 8px;">
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/#tiers">See tiers and pricing</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/guarantee">Read the guarantee</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Book a fit call</span>
      <h2>Decide from the numbers. Prove it in the cash.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        In 14 days you know what the practice's money is actually doing, in dollars: the traps that are running, the recoverable value, and the first three moves, whether or not we ever work together again. It starts with one 30-minute call.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={CALENDLY}>Book a fit call</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">See the 14-day Diagnostic</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-microcopy { font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); margin: 10px 0 0; }
  .promise-line { font-family: Inter, sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); margin-top: 8px; }
</style>
